<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea Exchange Bank to open in Warsaw.</title>
<headline>Korea Exchange Bank to open in Warsaw.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Korea Exchange Bank said on Wednesday it would open a representative office in Warsaw in June.</p>
<p>The bank said it obtained the approval from the Polish central bank, the National Bank of Poland, earlier this month, and was awaiting approval from Seoul's financial authorities.</p>
<p>The bank's Polish office will provide financial brokering and investment consulting services to South Korean companies operating in east European countries.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
